# The vendored oracle corpus is DATA, not source. Its bytes are the whole
# point: 10 of the 318 JSONTestSuite files carry deliberate CR and LF inside
# them, and with core.autocrlf on, git would store them normalised and hand a
# Linux checkout different bytes from a Windows one. The verdicts happen not
# to change -- that was measured, 318/318 either way -- but "we ran the corpus
# pinned at 1ef36fa" would stop being exactly true, and that is the claim.
oracle/** -text

# The captured C verdicts are compared line by line; leave them alone too.
oracle/corejson.trace -text

# --- GitHub Linguist: what is this project's code ---------------------------
#
# Every crate that ships from this repository is PURE RUST. Checked, not
# asserted: no crate under `crates/` has a build script, a `cc` or `bindgen`
# build-dependency, or a `links` key, so nothing here compiles C into a
# published artefact.
#
# The C, assembly, shell and Python below are the DIFFERENTIAL ORACLE, the
# benchmarks, the firmware examples' ABI gate and the release scripts. The
# pinned C is built as a dev-only reference and its trace is checked in --
# that harness is how every number in the README was measured, so it stays in
# the repository, but it is not what this project is written in.
#
# `linguist-detectable=false` rather than `linguist-vendored`: these files are
# ours, they are simply not the language of the product.

oracle/**            linguist-detectable=false
bench/**             linguist-detectable=false

*.sh                 linguist-detectable=false
*.py                 linguist-detectable=false

firmware/**/*.c      linguist-detectable=false
firmware/**/*.h      linguist-detectable=false
firmware/**/*.S      linguist-detectable=false
hosted/**/*.c        linguist-detectable=false
hosted/**/*.h        linguist-detectable=false
seam/*.c             linguist-detectable=false

# `memory.x` is a linker script. Linguist reads a bare `.x` as RPC, which is
# how "RPC" appeared in the language bar of four of these repositories.
*.x                  linguist-language=Linker Script
